  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the number of hexagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{number of hexagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of hexagons. There are $3$ hexagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $2:3.$",
